#!/bin/sh
# SPDX-License-Identifier: MPL-2.0
#
# Stands in for a program whose behavior a test needs to control.
#
# A test must never run a file it wrote itself. Writing an executable leaves a
# descriptor open for the length of the write, another thread's fork inherits
# it, and the kernel then refuses to exec that inode while any writer holds it
# — `ETXTBSY`, arriving only when the machine is loaded enough for the two to
# overlap. Sleeping, retrying, syncing, or renaming around it changes the odds
# rather than the ownership: the inode being executed is still one this
# process opened for writing.
#
# This file is checked in and never written at runtime, so no descriptor for
# it ever exists. A test installs it under whatever name it needs — a symlink
# creates no writable descriptor — and puts the behavior it wants beside that
# name in an ordinary data file.
#
# `$0` is the path the caller invoked, symlink and all, so `$0.behavior` is
# that file. Sourcing it rather than running it keeps this shell's arguments,
# working directory, process group, and PID, all of which are what the tests
# are actually observing.

. "$0.behavior"
